  "findings": [
    "An SIS infection (recovery 0.2 per step) becomes endemic on the faculty network once beta/mu exceeds about 0.054 (susceptibility peak; mean-field predictions: quenched 1/Lambda_max = 0.039, heterogeneous <k>/<k2> = 0.049), lower than 0.063 on degree-preserving rewired networks and 0.100 on Erdos-Renyi networks.",
    "At beta/mu = 0.081 (1.5x the threshold), a single infected faculty member's outbreak size correlates best with eigenvector centrality (Spearman rho = 0.95); k-shell gives 0.92 and degree 0.87.",
    "Seeding the most-connected faculty member reaches 34 faculty on average versus 10 from a random faculty member, with a major outbreak (>= 10% of faculty) in 62% vs 16% of runs.",
    "An outbreak started in one lab reaches a given other lab in 5% of runs on the observed network vs 23% on degree-preserving rewired networks; the largest gap is IGIB -> CDRI: 4% vs 31%.",
    "A random walker on the co-authorship network takes on average 147 steps to first reach another lab vs 10 on rewired networks (mean ratio 21.0x, range 5.0-40.9x).",
    "After 5 steps a walker started in a lab is still inside it with probability CCMB 0.60, IGIB 0.86, IMTECH 0.78, CDRI 0.97 vs 0.07, 0.16, 0.09, 0.67 on rewired networks.",
    "The walk's spectral gap is 0.017 (relaxation time 60 steps) vs 0.169 (7 steps) after rewiring: walks mix more slowly on the real network, as expected if labs act as communities.",
    "Adding 40 cross-lab collaborations raises cross-lab outbreak reach from 5% to 8% (random cross-lab), 10% (hub-to-hub), 7% (topic-similar), and lowers the mean cross-lab first-passage time from 147 to 95, 101, 100 steps."
  ],
  "methods": {
    "network": "faculty co-authorship graph, weight = joint papers with <= 50 authors; SIS sweep and random walks on the largest connected component",
    "nulls": "degree-preserving double-edge-swap rewiring (10 x E swaps; connected swaps with shuffled weights for random walks) and Erdos-Renyi G(n, m)",
    "sis": "discrete-time SIS, mu = 0.2, 25 lambda values, 100 replicas per lambda from one random seed, 500 burn-in + 500 measured steps, reactivation at one random node when extinct (quasi-stationary); survival = never went extinct",
    "threshold": "numeric = lambda at the peak of chi = N(<rho^2>-<rho>^2)/<rho>; HMF = <k>/<k^2>; QMF = 1/largest adjacency eigenvalue",
    "sir": "discrete-time SIR at beta = 0.0163, mu = 0.2 (beta/mu = 1.5 x observed numeric SIS threshold); 100 runs per seed node, 1000 per strategy",
    "crosslab": "SIR from a random node of each lab, 1000 runs per lab observed and over 10 rewired networks; reach = any new infection in the target lab",
    "random_walk": "weighted walk P = S^-1 W on the LCC; MFPT solved exactly; retention from the stationary distribution restricted to the lab; 20 connected rewired nulls; RWR restart 0.15 on the full graph",
    "interventions": "add k cross-lab edges (weight 1): random pairs (10 draws), largest degree product, or highest subfield cosine among never-co-authored pairs; 250 SIR runs per seed lab per draw"
  },
